    "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes protocol-relative URL resolution — the bug documented as **ADR-034's finding #2**. Small, focused, 4 tests.\n\n## The bug\n\nURLs starting with `//` (protocol-relative, e.g. `//thumb.wikimedia.org/.../Tim_Berners-Lee.jpg`) were falling through to relative resolution:\n\n```\nhref:  //thumb.wikimedia.org/.../Tim_Berners-Lee_April_2009.jpg\nbase:  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTML\n\nbefore: https://en.wikipedia.org//thumb.wikimedia.org/...  (404)\nafter:  https://thumb.wikimedia.org/...                     (correct)\n```\n\nThe leading `//` was being treated as a path prefix. Per RFC 3986 §4.2, protocol-relative URLs inherit the scheme from the base URL.\n\n## The fix\n\nTwo-line check at function entry:\n\n```cpp\nif (href.size() >= 2 && href[0] == '/' && href[1] == '/') {\n    if (base.rfind(\"http://\", 0) == 0) return \"http:\" + href;\n    return \"https:\" + href;\n}\n```\n\nDefault to `https:` for anything else (file:// base, schemeless base) since HTTPS is the right answer for 99% of real-world usage.\n\n## What this unblocks\n\nThe 3 below-fold `<img>` thumbnails in the HTML article:\n- Tim Berners-Lee photo (`//thumb.wikimedia.org/.../250px-Tim_Berners-Lee_April_2009.jpg`)\n- HTML5 logo (`//thumb.wikimedia.org/.../250px-HTML5_logo_and_wordmark.svg.png`)\n- HTML element categories diagram (`//thumb.wikimedia.org/.../250px-HTML_element_content_categories.svg.png`)\n\nPre-fix: fetch fails, `<img>` renders as empty box. Post-fix: fetch succeeds, decode succeeds. They'll render correctly **once ADR-035 gives images layout space** (currently they still overlap content below them, per ADR-034's v1 limitation).\n\n## Tests\n\n4 in `[url][protocol-relative]`:\n- `https://` base → `https:` prefix\n- `http://` base → `http:` prefix\n- schemeless base → `https:` default\n- absolute URL unaffected (regression)\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before: 421 cases / 1737 assertions\n- After: **425 cases / 1741 assertions** (+4 / +4)\n- Full suite all pass, zero warnings\n\n## Verification checklist\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `resolve_url(\"//host/x\", \"https://a/y\")` -> `https://host/x` | ✅ |\n| `resolve_url(\"//host/x\", \"http://a/y\")` -> `http://host/x` | ✅ |\n| `resolve_url(\"//host/x\", \"schemeless/y\")` -> `https://host/x` | ✅ |\n| Absolute URLs still pass through | ✅ (regression) |\n| Existing `[url][resolve]` tests unaffected | ✅ |\n| Full suite green (425 / 1741) | ✅ |\n\n## What's next\n\n**ADR-035** (layout-integrated `<img>`): sync fetch at layout time, intrinsic dims feed `box.height`, siblings flow correctly. With this fix landed, the 3 below-fold thumbnails will render without overlapping content. Highest remaining visible delta.\n\nRefs ADR-034 finding #2\n",
